  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1947, the FBI director J. Edgar Hoover wrote by hand on a bureau memo that \"we must insist upon full access to discs recovered,\" and complained that \"the Army grabbed it and wouldn't let the bureau have it for cursory examination.\" The UFO researcher and filmmaker James Fox points to the note, which also appears in his work Out of the Blue. He reads it as proof that a disc was recovered and that the Army kept it even from the FBI."
